tock management data through the framework's SWR cache\\n\\nhandleMutate called the global `mutate` exported by swr. That function is\\nbound to SWR's default cache. The framework's openmrsComponentDecorator\\nwraps every component in an SWRConfig whose provider is a shared,\\nmodule-level cache, and the useSWR hooks in this app read from that cache.\\nhandleMutate therefore matched no keys, so the table refresh actions and\\nthe revalidation after saves and deletes never refetched anything.\\n\\nReplace handleMutate with a useHandleMutate hook. The hook takes `mutate`\\nfrom useSWRConfig(), which is bound to the cache of the nearest SWRConfig,\\nand returns a function that revalidates every string key starting with the\\ngiven URL. The 16 components that called handleMutate now call the hook\\nand use the returned function. The call sites and URL prefixes are\\nunchanged. The returned function is added to the useCallback dependency\\narrays that reference it.\\n\\nAdd a test for useHandleMutate that renders useSWR under an SWRConfig with\\nits own cache provider and checks that only the matching key is refetched.\\nUpdate the stock items table and stock source delete tests to mock the\\nhook. The delete test now triggers the component's own onConfirmation\\nhandler instead of calling the mock directly.\\n\\n* Drop the redundant revalidate option from useHandleMutate\\n\\nSWR's mutate revalidates matched keys unless revalidate is explicitly false, so passing { revalidate: true } has no effect. The explicit undefined data argument stays, so the call still takes the same path through SWR's mutate.\\n\\n* Revalidate stock rules after saving a rule\\n\\nThe stock rule form is now a child workspace, so the stock item\\nworkspace stays mounted underneath it. Closing the rule form after a\\nsave returned to the Rules tab with the old list, because nothing\\nrevalidated the stock rule query.\\n\\nThe save handler now revalidates every stockmanagement/stockrule key\\nbefore closing. It uses the mutate from useSWRConfig rather than the\\nhandleMutate helper. handleMutate calls the global mutate exported by\\nswr, which is bound to SWR's default cache, while the framework gives\\ndecorated components their own shared cache. So handleMutate doesn't\\nreach the rule list's query.\\n\\n* Use useHandleMutate to revalidate stock rules after saving\\n\\nReplace the inline useSWRConfig().mutate call and its URL-prefix key filter with the useHandleMutate hook from src/utils.ts, which does the same revalidation through the framework's SWR cache. This matches how the rest of the app revalidates after saves and deletes.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9556d5a07c6263b485df10dda346f2ec47df5427\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T18:35:25+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Use framework modal for stock locations (#630)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Use framework modal for stock locations\\n\\nRegister the create-location dialog with the framework and pass the table refresh callback explicitly. Keep the existing workspace registration as an adapter.\\n\\nConnect the footer submit button to the location form and cover submission and cancellation.\\n\\n* Fix location modal cleanup and list refresh\\n\\nGuard modal disposal so workspace cleanup cannot close the workspace again. Pass the bound FHIR list mutator through the location hooks and use it after creation and for the table refresh action.\\n\\nAdd regression coverage for StrictMode cleanup, external closure, modal dismissal, and refresh callback propagation. All 122 tests, TypeScript, and lint pass.\\n\\n* fix: Keep the location form open when saving fails\\n\\nWait for location creation before closing the modal and disable Save while the request is pending. Keep entered values available for retry and use a simple refresh callback type.\\n\\nAdd regression coverage for pending saves, failed requests, and successful retries. All six focused tests and TypeScript pass.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"babd91e98530d3507d73c4bdbe9b60b735425c6b\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T15:47:48-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Remove a dead SCSS rule\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"54a026b5e680fedb3fc7eab6edb2f08097c88bf9\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T13:37:58-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Switch to using `useExtensionSlotMeta()` (#622)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"390dc57d290de305f41f5af1755fc8c59480407c\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T11:42:45+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Fix stock report generation, visibility, downloads, and role-based access (#616)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* Fix Stock Report Generation Visibility Downloads and Role Based Access\\n\\n* Fix Stock Report Generation Visibility Downloads and Role Based Access\\n\\n* Updated according to the review feedback.\\n\\n* Updated according to the review feedback.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Mwanje Musa\",\"authorEmail\":\"mwanjemusa@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"bc258af8e39f5377fa36b4c4573ff8b0f6460157\",\"date\":\"2026-08-11T19:13:24+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#605)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Lint config moves to a flat eslint.config.mjs that spreads\\n@openmrs/eslint-config 2.0.0, replacing .eslintrc. eslint moves from 8.57 to\\n^9.39.0 and the --ext flag goes away, since flat config makes it redundant.\\n\\nComparing the effective rule sets before and after, the overlay re-enables\\nwhat this repo enforced and the shared config turns off: triple-slash-reference,\\nno-extra-boolean-cast, no-prototype-builtins, no-unsafe-optional-chaining,\\nno-useless-escape, prefer-const, exhaustive-deps as a warning, and the three\\nrules typescript-eslint v8 split ban-types into.\\n\\nThe previous config applied testing-library's rules to every file rather\\nthan to tests. All 22 still apply to test files, where jest-dom now applies\\ntoo. They no longer apply to the rest of src, where they had nothing to\\nreport: those rules look for render and screen calls.\\n\\nThe shared config adds no-console, which this repo did not have. It found\\nthree console.info calls, two of them logging a caught error. Those are\\nconsole.error now, which is the level they belonged at. The third logs the\\noperation payload in a branch reached when no operation type matched, so it\\nis a console.warn.\\n\\ne2e was never covered by the lint script. It is now, which is where the\\nremaining reports came from: type-only imports made explicit, one blank line,\\nand a Playwright fixture. Fixtures take a callback named use and call it,\\nwhich eslint-plugin-react-hooks reads as React's use hook, so rules-of-hooks\\nis off for e2e.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3c071999ea6f2b75706d5ba602caeba07ec55a02\",\"date\":\"2026-07-06T18:26:40+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#566) (#567)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Josephkagimu1\",\"authorEmail\":\"88326256+Josephkagimu1@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"4a542bb184620adf4a130a72da5bd5ddc0b944a4\",\"date\":\"2026-05-28T20:17:17+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5703: Prevent \\\"Select source type\\\" label from wrapping in stock sources toolbar (#562)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Bawantha Thilan\",\"authorEmail\":\"38850236+Bawanthathilan@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c9d7c101c64554474c6b32c734789362166eaf37\",\"date\":\"2026-05-17T20:28:02+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5648: Wire up stock report submission and add missing patient/stock-item inputs (#542)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Lubwama Samuel\",\"authorEmail\":\"lubwamasamuel3@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1b6d419503165d7ca514c53dbe87ac1f256cf725\",\"date\":\"2026-05-13T17:32:40+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Migrate to rspack (#553)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Switch the bundler from webpack to rspack, matching the migration already\\nlanded across the rest of the distro.\\n\\n- Rename webpack.config.js to rspack.config.js and require\\n  openmrs/default-rspack-config\\n- Update package.json build/serve/analyze scripts to call rspack\\n- Drop @types/webpack-env and declare RequireContext + NodeJS.Require\\n  locally in declarations.d.ts so require.context still type-checks\\n- Drop the **/*.d.ts entry from .eslintignore (deleting the now-empty\\n  file) so the lint-staged eslint pass (which uses --max-warnings 0)\\n  does not flag declarations.d.ts as ignored. The file lints cleanly.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"79953cf66885a70e1b0430f14d82d9fb8b4de86e\",\"date\":\"2026-05-13T16:45:28+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#552)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\\n\\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest, aligning stock-management\\nwith the patterns adopted by openmrs-esm-core, openmrs-esm-billing-app,\\nand the other in-flight migrations.\\n\\n- Replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-cli, jest-environment-jsdom, and\\n  @types/jest with vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and cross-env;\\n  bump @testing-library/dom (10.4.0 to 10.4.1) and\\n  @testing-library/jest-dom (5.x to 6.x) so the /vitest subpath is\\n  available.\\n- Add vitest.config.ts with the standard O3 vitest setup: jsdom\\n  environment, .scss/.css aliased to identity-obj-proxy with an\\n  anchored ^.*.s?css$ regex, @openmrs/esm-framework aliased to its\\n  mock, react-i18next aliased to the local __mocks__ file, @mocks\\n  and @tools aliases for the path shortcuts already in use, and\\n  fakeTimers.toFake limited to the timers we actually fake (excludes\\n  queueMicrotask which otherwise breaks React's scheduler).\\n- Add tools/setup-tests.ts to load @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\\n  (which is enough for tsc to pick up the matcher type extension),\\n  register afterEach(cleanup), and rewrite the ResizeObserver mock\\n  as a class (Carbon's TextArea calls it with `new`).\\n- Convert the eighteen test files to the vitest API: explicit imports\\n  for describe/expect/it/test/vi (plus beforeEach where used), jest.*\\n  swapped for vi.*, jest.Mock type alias replaced with Mock from\\n  vitest. Inline component factories of the form vi.mock(name, () =>\\n  () => <jsx />) wrapped in { default: ... } since vitest requires\\n  the factory to return a module object. The vi.mock('./hooks/\\n  useParties', () => vi.fn()) factory similarly wrapped to expose a\\n  default export.\\n- Update the danger-button selector in stock-sources-delete.test.tsx\\n  to /danger\\\\s*delete/i: the newer testing-library no longer joins\\n  the visually-hidden \\\"danger\\\" prefix and the visible \\\"Delete\\\" with\\n  a space when computing the accessible name.\\n- Delete jest.config.js.\\n\\nAll 112 tests pass; lint and typescript checks are green.\\n\\n* (chore) Tidy up vitest config and test imports\\n\\nFollow-ups to the jest→vitest migration:\\n\\n- vitest.config.ts: drop `globals: true` (every test file imports\\n  describe/it/expect/vi/test explicitly, so the global is dead),\\n  drop the unused `@tools` alias (no `from '@tools'` in src), and\\n  add `resolve.mainFields: ['module', 'main']` so vitest picks\\n  @carbon/react's ESM entry. The CJS entry's `var l10n =\\n  require('flatpickr/dist/l10n/index')` only exposes `default`,\\n  leaving `l10n['en']` undefined and producing 300+ \\\"flatpickr:\\n  invalid locale undefined\\\" stderr lines per `--reporter=verbose`\\n  run.\\n- 10 test files: strip the unused `test` named import from the\\n  `vitest` import line. ESLint won't catch these because\\n  `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` is disabled in .eslintrc.\\n- 3 test files (step1, user-selector, stock-sources-items-table):\\n  drop redundant `__esModule: true` from `vi.mock` factory\\n  returns — vitest doesn't need the marker when the factory\\n  returns `{ default: ... }`.\\n\\n* (fix) Silence React warnings from stock-item-details\\n\\nTwo pre-existing warnings surfaced once vitest started routing\\nper-test stderr through its verbose reporter:\\n\\n1. `forwardRef render functions accept exactly two parameters` —\\n   StockItemDetails was wrapped in forwardRef but its render\\n   function only took `(props)` and no caller passed a ref. Drop\\n   the dead wrap and inline-type the props.\\n\\n2. `React does not recognize the 'controllerName' prop on a DOM\\n   element` — ControlledTextInput spread `{...props}` onto the\\n   inner Carbon `<TextInput>`, leaking the `controllerName` and\\n   `control` react-hook-form props through to the DOM `<input>`.\\n   Destructure them out before spreading. The sibling\\n   ControlledRadioButtonGroup already does this; the wrappers\\n   now agree.\\n\\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath for vitest config aliases\\n\\nvitest.config.ts used new URL(...).pathname for the react-i18next\\nand @mocks alias replacements. On Windows .pathname yields /C:/...\\nwhich is not a valid filesystem path, so Vite's resolver fails.\\nAdd a small fileURLToPath helper and route every URL-based path\\nthrough it, matching the pattern adopted in openmrs-esm-form-builder.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6ea904ad3ba59b17d8366d5cc3283f8968d416be\",\"date\":\"2026-05-07T22:00:44+05:30\",\"message\":\"fix(O3-5563): require purchase price packaging unit when purchase price is set (#528)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Kavitha Kanchana\",\"authorEmail\":\"146015143+kanchana404@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"d9e7c5c49d29b5b1dc37951adb3c2887916e4f48\",\"date\":\"2026-05-05T15:10:51+05:30\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5562: Edit Items panel fields don't update when selecting a different stock item (#514)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Wikum Weerakutti\",\"authorEmail\":\"wikum@linuxdeveloper.space\"},{\"hash\":\"c67e47060f34697bd5e9aa63389a35fc5df2eed8\",\"date\":\"2026-05-05T09:15:40+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) O3-5647: Fix User Role Scope Save Functionality (#541)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* O3-5647: Fix User Role Scope Save Functionality\\n\\n* Response to Comments\",\"authorName\":\"Lubwama Samuel\",\"authorEmail\":\"lubwamasamuel3@gmail.com\"}],\"totalCount\":16}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ku6cwQtu5452ULfuTDuBST","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
